{title: Come Thou Font}
{artist: Bethel Music}
{key: A}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
[A] [E] [D] [E] [A]

{comment: Verse 1}
Come, Thou [A]Fount of every [E]blessing, tune my [D]heart to [E]sing Thy [A]grace;
Streams of[A] mercy, never [E]ceasing, call for [D]songs of [E]loudest [A]praise.
Teach me[A/C#] some melodious sonnet, sung by f[D]laming tongues a[A]bove.
Praise the [A]mount! I'm fixed [E]upon it, Mount of [D]God's [E]redeeming [A]love.

{comment: Verse 2}
Here I [A]raise mine [E]Ebenezer; Hither [D]by Thy [E]help I'm [A]come;
And I [A]hope, by Thy good [E]pleasure, safely [D]to ar[E]rive at [A]home.
Jesus [A/C#]sought me when a stranger, wandering f[D]rom the fold of G[A]od;
He, to [A]rescue me from d[E]anger, inter[D]posed His [E]precious bl[A]ood.

{comment: Verse 3}
O to g[A]race how great a [E]debtor, daily [D]I'm con[E]strained to [A]be!
Let Th[A]y goodness, like a fe[E]tter, bind my w[D]andering [E]heart to [A]Thee.
